OrionLayer open fix 94 — the Energy Absorber's charge as a battle event
=======================================================================

Work order 259 (258 P2, Data: take the glow's start, duration and end from
the original source and make HD match it). orion2re on the fork's branch
`orionlayer` (v2.0.0), on top of open fix 93; commit 42f32654. Not on
`orionlayer-local`. Every line under ORION2RE_EXT.

The original draws the Energy Absorber's glow whenever a unit's
reflected_damage_pool is above 0 (Draw_Ship_, cmbtdrw1.cpp:2632-2637). The
pool is charged inside Apply_Ship_Damage_ (cmbtfire.cpp:776-791), which
Fire_Ship_ runs for every shot of a FIRE (:1323) BEFORE the FIRE's one
Beam_SFX_ loop (:1461): the glow is on from the loop's first frame. It is
emptied after the absorber's discharge has been drawn (:1858) and as its
side's turn begins (combat1.cpp:1088). The snapshot that follows a FIRE
reaches a client after the animation, so the client drew the glow late.

CEV_ABSORB (24): unit, the charge after, the change — recorded by
Combat_Note (open fix 82: it keeps open fix 79's tick count) where the
charge is taken and, when there was one, where each of the two clears
empties it. The game's play is unchanged: the event reports values that
exist there.

